#: .././io/fadvise.c:18
#, c-format
msgid ""
"\n"
" advise the page cache about expected I/O patterns on the current file\n"
"\n"
" Modifies kernel page cache behaviour when operating on the current file.\n"
" The range arguments are required by some advise commands ([*] below).\n"
" With no arguments, the POSIX_FADV_NORMAL advice is implied.\n"
" -d -- don't need these pages (POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED) [*]\n"
" -n -- data will be accessed once (POSIX_FADV_NOREUSE) [*]\n"
" -r -- expect random page references (POSIX_FADV_RANDOM)\n"
" -s -- expect sequential page references (POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL)\n"
" -w -- will need these pages (POSIX_FADV_WILLNEED) [*]\n"
" Notes: these interfaces are not supported in Linux kernels before 2.6.\n"
"   NORMAL sets the default readahead setting on the file.\n"
"   RANDOM sets the readahead setting on the file to zero.\n"
"   SEQUENTIAL sets double the default readahead setting on the file.\n"
"   WILLNEED and NOREUSE are equivalent, and force the maximum readahead.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
" ge sidcachen information om förväntade I/O-mönster för den aktuella filen\n"
"\n"
" Ändrar kärnans sidcachebeteende vid arbete med den aktuella filen.\n"
" Intervallargumenten krävs av vissa advise-kommandon ([*] nedan).\n"
" Om inga argument anges används rådet POSIX_FADV_NORMAL.\n"
" -d -- behöver inte dessa sidor (POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED) [*]\n"
" -n -- data läses en gång (POSIX_FADV_NOREUSE) [*]\n"
" -r -- förvänta slumpmässiga sidreferenser (POSIX_FADV_RANDOM)\n"
" -s -- förvänta sekventiella sidreferenser (POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL)\n"
" -w -- behöver dessa sidor (POSIX_FADV_WILLNEED) [*]\n"
" Observera: dessa gränssnitt stöds inte i Linux-kärnor före 2.6.\n"
"   NORMAL anger filens standardinställning för readahead.\n"
"   RANDOM anger noll som inställning för readahead.\n"
"   SEQUENTIAL anger dubbla standardinställningen för readahead.\n"
"   WILLNEED och NOREUSE är likvärdiga och tvingar fram maximal readahead.\n"
"\n"

